# The fleet manager's Signal transport, and the only non-stdlib runtime
# dependency in the project — read the note in MODULE.bazel before adding a
# second one. Optional in practice: sigbot.py imports it lazily, so nothing
# loads it until [fleet_manager] is enabled.
#
# The floor is the API src/issuefleet/sigbot.py binds to: ServiceClient(
# base_url, api_key=), .service(), .send(text, prefix=), .messages(after_id=,
# limit=), and .react(message_id, emoji) — the last added in 0.3.0, which is
# what raised this floor. sigbot.py degrades gracefully if an older client is
# somehow installed, so the floor documents intent rather than guarding a crash.
# requirements_lock.txt pins the exact version and its hash; regenerate it with
# `bazel run //:requirements` after editing this file.
sigbot-client>=0.3.0
